# Google Cloud API key with the Chrome UX Report API enabled.
#
#   console.cloud.google.com
#     -> APIs & Services -> Library -> "Chrome UX Report API" -> Enable
#     -> APIs & Services -> Credentials -> Create credentials -> API key
#
# Then restrict it: Edit API key -> API restrictions -> Chrome UX Report API.
# It is a bearer credential, so anyone holding it can spend your quota.
#
# CrUX does NOT accept OAuth or service-account credentials. Passing a bearer
# token returns 400 INVALID_ARGUMENT, the same error as a malformed request.
CRUX_API_KEY=
